{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\nNo source-grounded evidence for legal order, recommendation, execution, check, or closure authority is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind legal authority; no basis for order issuance.\n\n**R02: Hazard Triggers & Zone Sequencing**\n[S04] notes South Pass closes under smoke visibility below 150 meters and North Bridge excludes full-size buses above 54°C [S04]. No explicit fire triggers or forecast binding found in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Route constraints exist, but trigger logic is absent.\n*   **Qualifications:** Smoke and heat conditions invalidate routes post-plan.\n*   **Blockers:** Missing conservative fire/weather triggers; no expiry logic defined.\n\n**R03: Population Basis & Assistance Demand**\n[S03] specifies Zone A (5,280), B (8,940), C (12,600) residents plus up to 2,100 tourists [S03]. Survey coverage is 91% [S03]. Categories (no vehicle, mobility, oxygen, dialysis) overlap and must not be summed as independent people [S03].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted with qualification.\n*   **Qualifications:** Must carry uncertainty allowance for unreported households; cannot treat unregistered as self-evacuating [S03]. Tourist demand is time-dependent [S03].\n*   **Blockers:** Overlap logic must be enforced to avoid double-counting.\n\n**R04: Road Bottlenecks & Route Clearance**\n[S04] establishes Mill Junction as the system bottleneck with a measured sustainable throughput of 1,500 vehicles/hour [S04]. North Bridge (1,100 veh/h) and South Pass (850 veh/h) feed into Mill Junction; their capacities cannot be added [S04]. Last exercise achieved only 1,180 veh/h at Mill Junction due to unmanaged lane merging [S04].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not sum independent road ratings across the shared downstream bottleneck [S04]. Clearance time must use shared junction and exercise throughput until a current field test proves otherwise [S04].\n*   **Blockers:** Contraflow requires sheriff closure, 45 minutes setup, and staffed crossover points [S04]. County 12 cannot be fully converted to outbound traffic [S04].\n\n**R05: Fleet Matching & Driver Duty**\nNo evidence for person/accommodation-level fleet matching, driver duty cycles, bridge constraints specific to vehicle types (beyond S04 bus exclusion), or relief capacity is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind fleet requirements; no cycle time data available.\n\n**R06: Shelter Capacity & Medical Handoffs**\n[S07] identifies 73 oxygen users, 28 dialysis patients, and 14 refrigerated medication cases with 7 duplicate household records [S07]. Capacities total 79 only if transport, power, and patient matching pass [S07]. Generic shelter cots are not medical placements [S07]. No evidence for smoke-safe shelter capacity or accessible placements beyond medical needs is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Medical handoffs defined; general shelter capacity missing.\n*   **Qualifications:** Public status messages may not expose health needs [S07]. Private roster rules govern matching and deletion [S07].\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot verify general shelter suitability or power continuity.\n\n**R07: Warnings & Community Support**\n[S08] notes IPAWS reached 82% of enrolled devices in the last exercise, while sirens provided no zone-specific instruction [S08]. 9% of households primarily use Hmong and 6% require another language or ASL relay [S08]. Current IPAWS template is only English and Spanish [S08]. Door-knock teams cover mobile-home areas but need ninety minutes [S08]. County and volunteer-fire radios share voice but not unit identifiers until the interoperability gateway is configured and tested [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Channel metrics exist; language coverage and radio interoperability are deficient.\n*   **Qualifications:** Warning lead time must include translation and door-knock completion before the conservative clearance deadline [S08]. Communications failure can change the effective population departure curve in S03 [S08]. The same zone revision and effective time must appear across IPAWS, radio, hotline, and field teams to avoid contradictory movement [S08].\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot treat message transmission as evidence that the intended population received or understood it [S08]. A successful county-only radio check is insufficient [S08].\n\n**R08: Fuel & Power Continuity**\nNo evidence for fuel/power continuity, observed delays, local staging, alternate routes/suppliers, or coupled asset effects is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind resource contracting.\n\n**R09: Animals & Service Animals**\nNo evidence for animal handling or service animal separation without delaying human evacuation is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind animal logistics.\n\n**R10: Accountability & Data Privacy**\n[S07] requires person-level private matching with aggregate public reporting [S07]. Public status messages may not expose health needs [S07]. The private roster rules in S12 govern matching and deletion [S07]. No evidence for self-evacuation tracking, reconciliation, retention, or deletion proof is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Privacy constraints defined; operational tracking missing.\n*   **Qualifications:** Treat any unmatched oxygen, dialysis, or refrigerated-medication case as a blocker [S07].\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind full data management protocol.\n\n**R11: 48-Hour Execution Sequence**\nNo evidence for a concrete 48-hour sequence with owners, effects, current checks, repair, recheck, resource/cost authority, and contingencies is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind execution timeline.\n\n**R12: Verification & Readiness Blockers**\nNo evidence for exercise blockers, independent-review blockers, candidate-bound readiness, uncertainties, or explicit falsifiers is present in [S03], [S04], [S07], or [S08].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot verify readiness status.\n\n**Cross-Source Relationships & Contradictions**\n[S03] defines uncertain demand; [S04] defines supply constraints (road throughput, junction bottlenecks); [S07] defines medical continuity and accessibility matching; [S08] defines warning channels, language access, and radio interoperability. [S03] and [S04] are complementary but disjoint: [S03] defines demand while [S04] defines supply constraints. No contradictions exist between these sources. However, all four lack evidence for legal authority (R01), fleet specifics (R05), general shelter capacity (R06), communications strategy beyond current deficits (R07), resources (R08), animals (R09), data privacy beyond medical rosters (R10), execution sequence (R11), and verification (R12). The integration is incomplete for a full evacuation decision.\n\n**Unresolved Evidence**\n*   Specific trigger values for fire/weather (R02) are absent in [S03]/[S04]/[S07]/[S08].\n*   Fleet matching logic linking [S03] demand to vehicle capacity is absent.\n*   Shelter location and capacity data are entirely missing from provided sources."}}],"created":1787629074,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10434-7e4c0a968","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1880,"prompt_tokens":6434,"total_tokens":8314,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Szckzq0dG7HGMgWZTnZLDT2VRskKaImY","__verbose":{"index":0,"content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\nNo source-grounded evidence for l